IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mlr-core`
IMPORT `mlr2-helpers`
IMPORT `mlr2-ecdd`

-- CHAPTER 3 OF PART 3 -- SIMPLIFIED CUSTOMER DUE DILIGENCE (regulations 37 and 38) of the Money Laundering,
-- Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017 (S.I. 2017/692),
-- United Kingdom.  Lines 1170-1239 of the text.  The text is a plain-text rendering made by a converter
-- script; it is not the official text, and nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- LAYER 1: THE LAW, OBJECTIVELY.  A rule answers JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING (a MAYBE BOOLEAN):
-- JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words, NOTHING where it does not answer.
--
-- INPUTS THAT ANOTHER SECTION ANSWERS (seams, see NOTES.md "Seams (mlr2)"):
--   S-7, S-8   `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`   (regulation 8, part mlr1)
--   S-3 (internal to this part)   `reg 33(1) enhanced customer due diligence is required`, answered by mlr2-ecdd.l4

§ `Chapter 3 -- Simplified customer due diligence (regulations 37 and 38)`

§§ `Regulation 37 -- Application of simplified customer due diligence`

-- SEAM S-8 (asking).  The relevant person's own determination is an input of the core's `Level of risk`: the text hands the
-- judgement to the relevant person ("if it determines"), so it is never computed here.
-- src:1172 | (1) A relevant person may apply simplified customer due diligence measures in relation to a particular business relationship or transaction if it determines that the business relationship or transaction presents a low degree of risk of money laundering and terrorist financing, having taken into account—
-- src:1173 | (a) the risk assessment it carried out under regulation 18(1);
-- src:1174 | (b) relevant information made available to it under regulations 17(9) and 47; and
-- src:1175 | (c) the risk factors referred to in paragraph (3).
@ref reg 37(1) (src:1172-1175)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person's determination of the degree of risk of money laundering and terrorist financing that the business relationship or transaction presents` IS A `Level of risk`
      `it took into account the risk assessment it carried out under regulation 18(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it took into account relevant information made available to it under regulations 17(9) and 47` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it took into account the risk factors referred to in paragraph (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 37(1) the relevant person may apply simplified customer due diligence measures` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`
        (IF `the relevant person's determination of the degree of risk of money laundering and terrorist financing that the business relationship or transaction presents` EQUALS `low risk`
            AND `it took into account the risk assessment it carried out under regulation 18(1)`
            AND `it took into account relevant information made available to it under regulations 17(9) and 47`
            AND `it took into account the risk factors referred to in paragraph (3)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may apply simplified customer due diligence measures ... if it determines that the business relationship or transaction presents a low degree of risk ... having taken into account" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a) of NOTES.md)

-- reg 37(2): "Where a relevant person applies simplified customer due diligence measures, it must ..."
-- SEAM S-8 (asking)
-- src:1176 | (2) Where a relevant person applies simplified customer due diligence measures, it must—
-- src:1177 | (a) continue to comply with the requirements in regulations 28 , 29 and 30A, but it may adjust the extent, timing or type of the measures it undertakes under regulations 28 and 29(11) to (13) to reflect its determination under paragraph (1); and
@ref reg 37(2)(a) (src:1176-1177)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person applies simplified customer due diligence measures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 37(2)(a) the relevant person must continue to comply with the requirements in regulations 28, 29 and 30A` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`
        (IF `the relevant person applies simplified customer due diligence measures`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a relevant person applies simplified customer due diligence measures, it must" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- The permission to adjust: limited to the measures under regulations 28 and 29(11) to (13) and to the reflection of the paragraph (1) determination.
-- SEAM S-8 (asking)
-- src:1176 | (2) Where a relevant person applies simplified customer due diligence measures, it must—
-- src:1177 | (a) continue to comply with the requirements in regulations 28 , 29 and 30A, but it may adjust the extent, timing or type of the measures it undertakes under regulations 28 and 29(11) to (13) to reflect its determination under paragraph (1); and
@ref reg 37(2)(a) (src:1176-1177)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person applies simplified customer due diligence measures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measure is one undertaken under regulation 28 or under regulation 29(11) to (13)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the adjustment reflects the relevant person's determination under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 37(2)(a) the relevant person may adjust the extent, timing or type of the measure` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`
        (IF `the relevant person applies simplified customer due diligence measures`
            AND `the measure is one undertaken under regulation 28 or under regulation 29(11) to (13)`
            AND `the adjustment reflects the relevant person's determination under paragraph (1)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING) -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is of an adjustment "of the measures it undertakes under regulations 28 and 29(11) to (13) to reflect its determination under paragraph (1)"; the paragraph says nothing of any other adjustment

-- SEAM S-8 (asking)
-- src:1176 | (2) Where a relevant person applies simplified customer due diligence measures, it must—
-- src:1177 | (a) continue to comply with the requirements in regulations 28 , 29 and 30A, but it may adjust the extent, timing or type of the measures it undertakes under regulations 28 and 29(11) to (13) to reflect its determination under paragraph (1); and
-- src:1178 | (b) carry out sufficient monitoring of any business relationships or transactions which are subject to those measures to enable it to detect any unusual or suspicious transactions.
@ref reg 37(2)(b) (src:1176-1178)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person applies simplified customer due diligence measures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 37(2)(b) the relevant person must carry out sufficient monitoring of the business relationships or transactions subject to those measures` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`
        (IF `the relevant person applies simplified customer due diligence measures`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a relevant person applies simplified customer due diligence measures, it must" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- src:1179 | (3) When assessing whether there is a low degree of risk of money laundering and terrorist financing in a particular situation, and the extent to which it is appropriate to apply simplified customer due diligence measures in that situation, the relevant person must take account of risk factors including, among other things—
-- src:1180 | (a) customer risk factors, including whether the customer—
-- src:1181 | (i) is a public administration, or a publicly owned enterprise;
-- src:1182 | (ii) is an individual resident in a geographical area of lower risk (see sub-paragraph (c));
-- src:1183 | (iii) is a credit institution or a financial institution which is—
-- src:1184 | (aa) subject to requirements in national legislation having an equivalent effect to those laid down in the fourth money laundering directive on an obliged entity (within the meaning of that directive); and
-- src:1185 | (bb) supervised for compliance with those requirements in a manner equivalent to section 2 of Chapter VI of the fourth money laundering directive;
-- src:1186 | (iv) is a company whose securities are listed on a regulated market, and the location of the regulated market;
-- src:1187 | (b) product, service, transaction or delivery channel risk factors, including whether the product or service is—
-- src:1188 | (i) a life insurance policy for which the premium is low;
-- src:1189 | (ii) an insurance policy for a pension scheme which does not provide for an early surrender option, and cannot be used as collateral;
-- src:1190 | (iii) a pension, superannuation or similar scheme which satisfies the following conditions—
-- src:1191 | (aa) the scheme provides retirement benefits to employees;
-- src:1192 | (bb) contributions to the scheme are made by way of deductions from wages; and
-- src:1193 | (cc) the scheme rules do not permit the assignment of a member's interest under the scheme;
-- src:1194 | (iv) a financial product or service that provides appropriately defined and limited services to certain types of customers to increase access for financial inclusion purposes in the United Kingdom;
-- src:1195 | (v) a product where the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing are managed by other factors such as purse limits or transparency of ownership;
-- src:1196 | (vi) a child trust fund within the meaning given by section 1(2) of the Child Trust Funds Act 2004 ;
-- src:1197 | (vii) a junior ISA within the meaning given by regulation 2B of the Individual Savings Account Regulations 1998 ;
-- src:1198 | (c) geographical risk factors, including whether the country where the customer is resident, established or registered or in which it operates is—
-- src:1199 | (i) the United Kingdom;
-- src:1200 | (ii) a third country which has effective systems to counter money laundering and terrorist financing;
-- src:1201 | (iii) a third country identified by credible sources as having a low level of corruption or other criminal activity, such as terrorism (within the meaning of section 1 of the Terrorism Act 2000 ), money laundering, and the production and supply of illicit drugs;
-- src:1202 | (iv) a third country which, on the basis of credible sources, such as evaluations, detailed assessment reports or published follow-up reports published by the Financial Action Task Force, the International Monetary Fund, the World Bank, the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development or other international bodies or non-governmental organisations—
-- src:1203 | (aa) has requirements to counter money laundering and terrorist financing that are consistent with the revised Recommendations published by the Financial Action Task Force in February 2012 and updated in October 2016; and
-- src:1204 | (bb) effectively implements those Recommendations.
@ref reg 37(3) (src:1179-1204)
DECLARE `reg 37(3) risk factor` IS ONE OF
    `reg 37(3)(a)(i) is a public administration, or a publicly owned enterprise`
    `reg 37(3)(a)(ii) is an individual resident in a geographical area of lower risk`
    `reg 37(3)(a)(iii) is a credit institution or a financial institution`
    `reg 37(3)(a)(iv) is a company whose securities are listed on a regulated market`
    `reg 37(3)(b)(i) a life insurance policy for which the premium is low`
    `reg 37(3)(b)(ii) an insurance policy for a pension scheme which does not provide`
    `reg 37(3)(b)(iii) a pension, superannuation or similar scheme which satisfies`
    `reg 37(3)(b)(iv) a financial product or service that provides appropriately defined`
    `reg 37(3)(b)(v) a product where the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing`
    `reg 37(3)(b)(vi) a child trust fund within the meaning given by section 1(2)`
    `reg 37(3)(b)(vii) a junior ISA within the meaning given by regulation 2B`
    `reg 37(3)(c)(i) the United Kingdom`
    `reg 37(3)(c)(ii) a third country which has effective systems to counter money laundering`
    `reg 37(3)(c)(iii) a third country identified by credible sources as having a low level`
    `reg 37(3)(c)(iv) a third country which, on the basis of credible sources`
    `reg 37(3) another risk factor`

@ref reg 37(3) (src:1179-1204)
GIVETH A LIST OF `reg 37(3) risk factor`
`reg 37(3) the entries listed` MEANS LIST
      `reg 37(3)(a)(i) is a public administration, or a publicly owned enterprise`
    , `reg 37(3)(a)(ii) is an individual resident in a geographical area of lower risk`
    , `reg 37(3)(a)(iii) is a credit institution or a financial institution`
    , `reg 37(3)(a)(iv) is a company whose securities are listed on a regulated market`
    , `reg 37(3)(b)(i) a life insurance policy for which the premium is low`
    , `reg 37(3)(b)(ii) an insurance policy for a pension scheme which does not provide`
    , `reg 37(3)(b)(iii) a pension, superannuation or similar scheme which satisfies`
    , `reg 37(3)(b)(iv) a financial product or service that provides appropriately defined`
    , `reg 37(3)(b)(v) a product where the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing`
    , `reg 37(3)(b)(vi) a child trust fund within the meaning given by section 1(2)`
    , `reg 37(3)(b)(vii) a junior ISA within the meaning given by regulation 2B`
    , `reg 37(3)(c)(i) the United Kingdom`
    , `reg 37(3)(c)(ii) a third country which has effective systems to counter money laundering`
    , `reg 37(3)(c)(iii) a third country identified by credible sources as having a low level`
    , `reg 37(3)(c)(iv) a third country which, on the basis of credible sources`

-- reg 37(3): the risk factors a relevant person must take account of when assessing whether there is a low degree of risk (customer, product and geographical factors).
@ref reg 37(3) (src:1179-1204)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 37(3) risk factor`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 37(3) the relevant person must take the risk factor into account` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 37(3)(a)(i) is a public administration, or a publicly owned enterprise` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 37(3)(a)(ii) is an individual resident in a geographical area of lower risk` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 37(3)(a)(iii) is a credit institution or a financial institution` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 37(3)(a)(iv) is a company whose securities are listed on a regulated market` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 37(3)(b)(i) a life insurance policy for which the premium is low` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 37(3)(b)(ii) an insurance policy for a pension scheme which does not provide` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 37(3)(b)(iii) a pension, superannuation or similar scheme which satisfies` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 37(3)(b)(iv) a financial product or service that provides appropriately defined` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 37(3)(b)(v) a product where the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 37(3)(b)(vi) a child trust fund within the meaning given by section 1(2)` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 37(3)(b)(vii) a junior ISA within the meaning given by regulation 2B` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 37(3)(c)(i) the United Kingdom` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 37(3)(c)(ii) a third country which has effective systems to counter money laundering` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 37(3)(c)(iii) a third country identified by credible sources as having a low level` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 37(3)(c)(iv) a third country which, on the basis of credible sources` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must take account of risk factors including, among other things"
    WHEN `reg 37(3) another risk factor` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "including, among other things" leaves other risk factors open

@ref reg 37(3) (src:1179-1204)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 37(3) risk factor`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`reg 37(3) the wording of the entry` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 37(3)(a)(i) is a public administration, or a publicly owned enterprise` THEN JUST "is a public administration, or a publicly owned enterprise"
    WHEN `reg 37(3)(a)(ii) is an individual resident in a geographical area of lower risk` THEN JUST "is an individual resident in a geographical area of lower risk (see sub-paragraph (c))"
    WHEN `reg 37(3)(a)(iii) is a credit institution or a financial institution` THEN JUST "is a credit institution or a financial institution which is— (aa) subject to requirements in national legislation having an equivalent effect to those laid down in the fourth money laundering directive on an obliged entity (within the meaning of that directive); and (bb) supervised for compliance with those requirements in a manner equivalent to section 2 of Chapter VI of the fourth money laundering directive"
    WHEN `reg 37(3)(a)(iv) is a company whose securities are listed on a regulated market` THEN JUST "is a company whose securities are listed on a regulated market, and the location of the regulated market"
    WHEN `reg 37(3)(b)(i) a life insurance policy for which the premium is low` THEN JUST "a life insurance policy for which the premium is low"
    WHEN `reg 37(3)(b)(ii) an insurance policy for a pension scheme which does not provide` THEN JUST "an insurance policy for a pension scheme which does not provide for an early surrender option, and cannot be used as collateral"
    WHEN `reg 37(3)(b)(iii) a pension, superannuation or similar scheme which satisfies` THEN JUST "a pension, superannuation or similar scheme which satisfies the following conditions— (aa) the scheme provides retirement benefits to employees; (bb) contributions to the scheme are made by way of deductions from wages; and (cc) the scheme rules do not permit the assignment of a member's interest under the scheme"
    WHEN `reg 37(3)(b)(iv) a financial product or service that provides appropriately defined` THEN JUST "a financial product or service that provides appropriately defined and limited services to certain types of customers to increase access for financial inclusion purposes in the United Kingdom"
    WHEN `reg 37(3)(b)(v) a product where the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing` THEN JUST "a product where the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing are managed by other factors such as purse limits or transparency of ownership"
    WHEN `reg 37(3)(b)(vi) a child trust fund within the meaning given by section 1(2)` THEN JUST "a child trust fund within the meaning given by section 1(2) of the Child Trust Funds Act 2004"
    WHEN `reg 37(3)(b)(vii) a junior ISA within the meaning given by regulation 2B` THEN JUST "a junior ISA within the meaning given by regulation 2B of the Individual Savings Account Regulations 1998"
    WHEN `reg 37(3)(c)(i) the United Kingdom` THEN JUST "the United Kingdom"
    WHEN `reg 37(3)(c)(ii) a third country which has effective systems to counter money laundering` THEN JUST "a third country which has effective systems to counter money laundering and terrorist financing"
    WHEN `reg 37(3)(c)(iii) a third country identified by credible sources as having a low level` THEN JUST "a third country identified by credible sources as having a low level of corruption or other criminal activity, such as terrorism (within the meaning of section 1 of the Terrorism Act 2000 ), money laundering, and the production and supply of illicit drugs"
    WHEN `reg 37(3)(c)(iv) a third country which, on the basis of credible sources` THEN JUST "a third country which, on the basis of credible sources, such as evaluations, detailed assessment reports or published follow-up reports published by the Financial Action Task Force, the International Monetary Fund, the World Bank, the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development or other international bodies or non-governmental organisations— (aa) has requirements to counter money laundering and terrorist financing that are consistent with the revised Recommendations published by the Financial Action Task Force in February 2012 and updated in October 2016; and (bb) effectively implements those Recommendations"
    WHEN `reg 37(3) another risk factor` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): the text gives no wording for a case it does not list

-- reg 37(3): "When assessing ... the relevant person must take account of risk factors including, among other things".
-- SEAM S-8 (asking)
@ref reg 37(3) (src:1179-1204)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person is assessing whether there is a low degree of risk of money laundering and terrorist financing in a particular situation, and the extent to which it is appropriate to apply simplified customer due diligence measures` IS A BOOLEAN
      item IS A `reg 37(3) risk factor`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 37(3) the relevant person must take account of the risk factor when assessing` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`
        (IF `the relevant person is assessing whether there is a low degree of risk of money laundering and terrorist financing in a particular situation, and the extent to which it is appropriate to apply simplified customer due diligence measures`
         THEN `reg 37(3) the relevant person must take the risk factor into account` item
         ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When assessing whether there is a low degree of risk of money laundering and terrorist financing" ("when" counts as "where": a condition that fails gives no, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- reg 37(3)(b)(iii): the scheme that is a low-risk product factor "satisfies the following conditions" (aa) to (cc).
-- src:1190 | (iii) a pension, superannuation or similar scheme which satisfies the following conditions—
-- src:1191 | (aa) the scheme provides retirement benefits to employees;
-- src:1192 | (bb) contributions to the scheme are made by way of deductions from wages; and
-- src:1193 | (cc) the scheme rules do not permit the assignment of a member's interest under the scheme;
@ref reg 37(3)(b)(iii) (src:1190-1193)
GIVEN `the scheme provides retirement benefits to employees` IS A BOOLEAN
      `contributions to the scheme are made by way of deductions from wages` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the scheme rules do not permit the assignment of a member's interest under the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 37(3)(b)(iii) the scheme satisfies the conditions` MEANS
    IF `the scheme provides retirement benefits to employees`
       AND `contributions to the scheme are made by way of deductions from wages`
       AND `the scheme rules do not permit the assignment of a member's interest under the scheme`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a pension, superannuation or similar scheme which satisfies the following conditions" (aa), (bb) and (cc), joined by "and": a scheme that fails one is not within (iii)

-- reg 37(4): "may not always indicate" -- the presence of risk factors does not decide the question either way.
-- src:1205 | (4) In making the assessment referred to in paragraph (3), relevant persons must bear in mind that the presence of one or more risk factors may not always indicate that there is a low risk of money laundering and terrorist financing in a particular situation.
@ref reg 37(4) (src:1205-1205)
GIVEN `the number of risk factors present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 37(4) the presence of the risk factors indicates a low risk of money laundering and terrorist financing` MEANS
    IF `the number of risk factors present` AT LEAST 1
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the presence of one or more risk factors may not always indicate that there is a low risk"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph speaks of "one or more risk factors"; it says nothing where none is present

-- reg 37(6): who paragraph (5) can be used for.  Paragraph (5) applies "where the customer is a person to whom paragraph (6) applies", so the list in (6) closes the class (fork F37-1).
-- SEAM S-7 (asking)
-- src:1209 | (6) This paragraph applies to—
-- src:1210 | (a) a relevant person who is subject to these Regulations under regulation 8;
-- src:1211 | (b) a person who carries on business in a third country who is—
-- src:1212 | (i) subject to requirements in national legislation having an equivalent effect to those laid down in the fourth money laundering directive on an obliged entity (within the meaning of that directive); and
-- src:1213 | (ii) supervised for compliance with those requirements in a manner equivalent to section 2 of Chapter VI of the fourth money laundering directive.
@ref reg 37(6) (src:1209-1213)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person carries on business in a third country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is subject to requirements in national legislation having an equivalent effect to those laid down in the fourth money laundering directive on an obliged entity (within the meaning of that directive)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is supervised for compliance with those requirements in a manner equivalent to section 2 of Chapter VI of the fourth money laundering directive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 37(6) paragraph (5) applies to the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person carries on business in a third country`
           AND `the person is subject to requirements in national legislation having an equivalent effect to those laid down in the fourth money laundering directive on an obliged entity (within the meaning of that directive)`
           AND `the person is supervised for compliance with those requirements in a manner equivalent to section 2 of Chapter VI of the fourth money laundering directive`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a relevant person is regulation 8's answer and has not been given
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): paragraph (5) operates "where the customer is a person to whom paragraph (6) applies", so the persons that paragraph (6) lists are the persons it reaches; a person who is neither a relevant person under regulation 8 nor a supervised third-country firm is in neither (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b); fork F37-1)

-- reg 37(5): the pooled account.
-- SEAM S-8 (asking)
-- src:1206 | (5) A relevant person may apply simplified customer due diligence measures where the customer is a person to whom paragraph (6) applies and the product is an account into which monies are pooled (the “pooled account”), provided that—
-- src:1207 | (a) the business relationship with the holder of the pooled account presents a low degree of risk of money laundering and terrorist financing; and
-- src:1208 | (b) information on the identity of the persons on whose behalf monies are held in the pooled account is available, on request to the relevant person where the pooled account is held.
@ref reg 37(5) (src:1206-1208)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (5) applies to the customer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the product is an account into which monies are pooled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the business relationship with the holder of the pooled account presents a low degree of risk of money laundering and terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `information on the identity of the persons on whose behalf monies are held in the pooled account is available, on request to the relevant person where the pooled account is held` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 37(5) the relevant person may apply simplified customer due diligence measures to the pooled account` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`
        (`mlr2 both are true` `paragraph (5) applies to the customer`
            (`mlr2 both are true` (`mlr2 the fact stated` `the product is an account into which monies are pooled`)
                (`mlr2 both are true`
                    (`mlr2 the fact stated` `the business relationship with the holder of the pooled account presents a low degree of risk of money laundering and terrorist financing`)
                    (`mlr2 the fact stated` `information on the identity of the persons on whose behalf monies are held in the pooled account is available, on request to the relevant person where the pooled account is held`))))
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the customer is a person to whom paragraph (6) applies and the product is an account into which monies are pooled" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)); and "provided that" the business relationship presents a low degree of risk and the identity information is available (a failed proviso, marginal reading (a))

-- reg 37(8): "must not continue to apply".  A flat negative: the answer to "may it continue?" is the text's no (ruling N2).
-- SEAM S-8 (asking); SEAM S-3 (internal): the limb (d) answer is `reg 33(1) enhanced customer due diligence is required`.
-- src:1215 | (8) A relevant person must not continue to apply simplified customer due diligence measures under paragraph (1)—
-- src:1216 | (a) if it doubts the veracity or accuracy of any documents or information previously obtained for the purposes of identification or verification;
-- src:1217 | (b) if its risk assessment changes and it no longer considers that there is a low degree of risk of money laundering and terrorist financing;
-- src:1218 | (c) if it suspects money laundering or terrorist financing; or
-- src:1219 | (d) if any of the conditions set out in regulation 33(1) apply.
@ref reg 37(8) (src:1215-1219)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it doubts the veracity or accuracy of any documents or information previously obtained for the purposes of identification or verification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its risk assessment changes and it no longer considers that there is a low degree of risk of money laundering and terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it suspects money laundering or terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 33(1) enhanced customer due diligence is required` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 37(8) the relevant person may continue to apply simplified customer due diligence measures under paragraph (1)` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`
        (BRANCH
            IF `it doubts the veracity or accuracy of any documents or information previously obtained for the purposes of identification or verification`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not continue to apply simplified customer due diligence measures ... if it doubts the veracity or accuracy of any documents or information"
            IF `its risk assessment changes and it no longer considers that there is a low degree of risk of money laundering and terrorist financing`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not continue ... if its risk assessment changes and it no longer considers that there is a low degree of risk"
            IF `it suspects money laundering or terrorist financing`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not continue ... if it suspects money laundering or terrorist financing"
            IF `reg 33(1) enhanced customer due diligence is required` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not continue ... if any of the conditions set out in regulation 33(1) apply"
            OTHERWISE NOTHING) -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is of continuing in the four cases (a) to (d); the paragraph says nothing of any other case

DECLARE `reg 37(8) party` IS ONE OF
    `reg 37(8) a relevant person`

DECLARE `reg 37(8) act` IS ONE OF
    `reg 37(8) continue to apply simplified customer due diligence measures under paragraph (1) after a doubt, a change of assessment, a suspicion or a regulation 33(1) condition`

@ref reg 37(8) (src:1215-1219)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `reg 37(8) party` `reg 37(8) act`
`reg 37(8) a relevant person must not continue to apply simplified customer due diligence measures` MEANS
    PARTY `reg 37(8) a relevant person`
    SHANT `reg 37(8) continue to apply simplified customer due diligence measures under paragraph (1) after a doubt, a change of assessment, a suspicion or a regulation 33(1) condition`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "a relevant person continued to apply simplified customer due diligence measures after one of the cases in regulation 37(8)(a) to (d) arose"

§§ `Regulation 38 -- Electronic money`

-- reg 38(1): the disapplication.  "Subject to paragraph (3)": paragraph (3) puts a monitoring duty on the issuer; it does not add a condition
-- to the disapplication (fork F38-3).  "The maximum amount ... is £150" is read as "is no more than £150" (fork F38-2).
-- "(ii) is subject to a maximum limit on monthly payment transactions of £150 which can only be used in the United Kingdom": the words
-- "which can only be used in the United Kingdom" are read as describing the payment instrument (fork F38-1).
-- SEAM S-8 (asking); this is the answer the plan (section 5.4) names `reg 38(1) the relevant person is not required to apply customer due diligence measures in relation to electronic money`.
-- src:1221 | (1) Subject to paragraph (3), a relevant person is not required to apply customer due diligence measures in relation to electronic money, and regulations 27, 28, 30 and 33 to 37 do not apply provided that—
-- src:1222 | (a) the maximum amount which can be stored electronically is £150;
-- src:1223 | (b) the payment instrument used in connection with the electronic money (“the relevant payment instrument”) is—
-- src:1224 | (i) not reloadable; or
-- src:1225 | (ii) is subject to a maximum limit on monthly payment transactions of £150 which can only be used in the United Kingdom;
-- src:1226 | (c) the relevant payment instrument is used exclusively to purchase goods or services;
-- src:1227 | (d) anonymous electronic money cannot be used to fund the relevant payment instrument.
@ref reg 38(1) (src:1221-1227)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the maximum amount which can be stored electronically, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the relevant payment instrument is not reloadable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant payment instrument is subject to a maximum limit on monthly payment transactions, in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the relevant payment instrument can only be used in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant payment instrument is used exclusively to purchase goods or services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `anonymous electronic money cannot be used to fund the relevant payment instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 38(1) the relevant person is not required to apply customer due diligence measures in relation to electronic money` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`
        (IF `the maximum amount which can be stored electronically, in pounds` AT MOST 150
            AND (`the relevant payment instrument is not reloadable` OR `the monthly limit is at most 150 and the instrument can only be used in the United Kingdom`)
            AND `the relevant payment instrument is used exclusively to purchase goods or services`
            AND `anonymous electronic money cannot be used to fund the relevant payment instrument`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not required to apply customer due diligence measures in relation to electronic money ... provided that" the four conditions hold (a failed proviso, marginal reading (a))
    WHERE
        `the monthly limit is at most 150 and the instrument can only be used in the United Kingdom` MEANS
            (CONSIDER `the relevant payment instrument is subject to a maximum limit on monthly payment transactions, in pounds`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
             WHEN JUST limit THEN limit AT MOST 150)
            AND `the relevant payment instrument can only be used in the United Kingdom`

-- The effect: "regulations 27, 28, 30 and 33 to 37 do not apply".  The regulation is named by its number.
@ref reg 38(1) (src:1221-1221)
GIVEN `the disapplication in regulation 38(1) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the number of the regulation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 38(1) the regulation does not apply in relation to the electronic money` MEANS
    IF `the number of the regulation` EQUALS 27 OR `the number of the regulation` EQUALS 28 OR `the number of the regulation` EQUALS 30
       OR (`the number of the regulation` AT LEAST 33 AND `the number of the regulation` AT MOST 37)
    THEN `the disapplication in regulation 38(1) applies`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph disapplies "regulations 27, 28, 30 and 33 to 37" and no other

-- reg 38(2): redemption in cash or cash withdrawal.
-- src:1228 | (2) Paragraph (1) does not apply to any transaction which consists of the redemption in cash, or a cash withdrawal, of the monetary value of the electronic money, where—
-- src:1229 | (a) the amount redeemed exceeds £50; or
-- src:1230 | (b) in the case of remote payment transactions, the amount redeemed exceeds £50 per transaction.
@ref reg 38(2) (src:1228-1230)
GIVEN `the transaction consists of the redemption in cash, or a cash withdrawal, of the monetary value of the electronic money` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount redeemed, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the transaction is a remote payment transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount redeemed per transaction, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 38(2) paragraph (1) does not apply to the transaction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the transaction consists of the redemption in cash, or a cash withdrawal, of the monetary value of the electronic money`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any transaction which consists of the redemption in cash, or a cash withdrawal, of the monetary value of the electronic money"
        IF `the amount redeemed, in pounds` GREATER THAN 50
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the transaction is a remote payment transaction` AND `the amount redeemed per transaction, in pounds` GREATER THAN 50
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not apply to any transaction which consists of the redemption ... where the amount redeemed exceeds £50" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- reg 38(3): the issuer's monitoring duty.
-- src:1231 | (3) The issuer of the relevant payment instrument must carry out sufficient monitoring of its business relationship with the users of electronic money and of transactions made using the relevant payment instrument to enable it to detect any unusual or suspicious transactions.
@ref reg 38(3) (src:1231-1231)
GIVEN `the person is the issuer of the relevant payment instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 38(3) the issuer must carry out sufficient monitoring of its business relationship with the users of electronic money and of transactions made using the relevant payment instrument` MEANS
    IF `the person is the issuer of the relevant payment instrument`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The issuer of the relevant payment instrument must"; the paragraph says nothing of anyone else

-- reg 38(4): simplified customer due diligence is still possible where the paragraph (1) conditions are not satisfied.
-- SEAM S-8 (asking); the permission under regulation 37 is this part's own answer, `reg 37(1) the relevant person may apply simplified customer due diligence measures`.
-- src:1232 | (4) A relevant person is not prevented from applying simplified customer due diligence measures in relation to electronic money because the conditions set out in paragraph (1) are not satisfied, provided that such measures are permitted under regulation 37.
@ref reg 38(4) (src:1232-1232)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the conditions set out in paragraph (1) are not satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 37(1) the relevant person may apply simplified customer due diligence measures` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 38(4) the relevant person is not prevented from applying simplified customer due diligence measures in relation to electronic money` MEANS
    `mlr2 for a relevant person` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`
        (IF `the conditions set out in paragraph (1) are not satisfied`
         THEN `reg 37(1) the relevant person may apply simplified customer due diligence measures`
         ELSE NOTHING) -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of the case where "the conditions set out in paragraph (1) are not satisfied"; where they are satisfied it says nothing
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provided that such measures are permitted under regulation 37" -- the regulation 37 answer is passed through unchanged, so a "no" there is a "no" here

-- reg 38(4A): acquirers and anonymous prepaid cards issued in a third country.  "shall only accept payment where": the word "only" closes it.
-- src:1233 | (4A) Credit institutions and financial institutions, acting as acquirers for payment using an anonymous prepaid card issued in a third country, shall only accept payment where—
-- src:1234 | (a) the anonymous prepaid card is subject to requirements in national legislation having an equivalent effect to those laid down in this regulation; and
-- src:1235 | (b) the anonymous prepaid card satisfies those requirements.
@ref reg 38(4A) (src:1233-1235)
GIVEN `the kind of institution` IS A `Kind of relevant person`
      `the institution is acting as an acquirer for payment using an anonymous prepaid card issued in a third country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the anonymous prepaid card is subject to requirements in national legislation having an equivalent effect to those laid down in this regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the anonymous prepaid card satisfies those requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 38(4A) the institution may accept payment using the anonymous prepaid card` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the kind of institution` EQUALS `credit institution` OR `the kind of institution` EQUALS `financial institution`))
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Credit institutions and financial institutions"
        IF (NOT `the institution is acting as an acquirer for payment using an anonymous prepaid card issued in a third country`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "acting as acquirers for payment using an anonymous prepaid card issued in a third country"
        IF `the anonymous prepaid card is subject to requirements in national legislation having an equivalent effect to those laid down in this regulation` AND `the anonymous prepaid card satisfies those requirements`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall only accept payment where" the card is subject to equivalent requirements and satisfies them

-- reg 38(5)(a): "acquirer" means ...
-- src:1236 | (5) For the purposes of this regulation—
@ref reg 38(5) (src:1236-1236)
-- src:1237 | (a) “acquirer” means a payment service provider contracting with a payee to accept and process card-based payment transactions, which result in a transfer of funds to the payee;
@ref reg 38(5)(a) (src:1237-1237)
GIVEN `the person is a payment service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it contracts with a payee to accept and process card-based payment transactions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those transactions result in a transfer of funds to the payee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 38(5)(a) the person is an acquirer` MEANS
    IF `the person is a payment service provider` AND `it contracts with a payee to accept and process card-based payment transactions` AND `those transactions result in a transfer of funds to the payee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'acquirer' means"

-- reg 38(5)(b) and (c): two terms that the paragraph defines by pointing at another instrument.
DECLARE `reg 38(5) term` IS ONE OF
    `reg 38(5)(b) payment instrument`
    `reg 38(5)(c) remote payment transaction`

-- src:1238 | (b) “payment instrument” has the meaning given by regulation 2(1) of the Electronic Money Regulations 2011;
-- src:1239 | (c) “remote payment transaction” has the meaning given by regulation 2 of the Payment Services Regulations 2017.
@ref reg 38(5)(b) and (c) (src:1238-1239)
GIVEN term IS A `reg 38(5) term`
GIVETH A STRING
`reg 38(5) the meaning of the term is given by` MEANS
    CONSIDER term
    WHEN `reg 38(5)(b) payment instrument` THEN "regulation 2(1) of the Electronic Money Regulations 2011"
    WHEN `reg 38(5)(c) remote payment transaction` THEN "regulation 2 of the Payment Services Regulations 2017"
